From 03f3f60114fa92d3d1be191bfc17106036cbffc2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nio <ddnio777@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 12:32:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] claudetui: the tap tells each main reply's allowance headers,
 so a setup-token account's 5h and 7d are known in interactive mode
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A `claude setup-token` account's allowance stayed "剩余额度未知" in magpie
with the bridge in interactive mode, the default: on a NAS gateway
(x86_64, Claude Code 2.1.309) its card never showed a window, however
many replies went through it. #2392, jsk644102-art, saw the same on
0.1.2627 and pointed at the cause and at tap.js as the place to fix it.

Why: such a token has the inference scope only, so `/usage` is never run
for it (errClaudeSetupToken) and only replies can tell its windows. In
interactive mode the helper learns them from the transcript, which keeps
`rate_limit_info` only on a `<synthetic>` API error row, a request turned
away. Every `/v1/messages` reply carries them in its
`anthropic-ratelimit-unified-*` headers; `-p` tells them as a
`rate_limit_event`, the interactive path never did.

- tap.js: for each main-turn `/v1/messages` reply, streamed or not, it
  writes `{limits}`, the reply's `anthropic-ratelimit-unified-*` headers
  keyed without that prefix.
- tap.go: a `{limits}` line is told as the `rate_limit_event` `-p` tells
  for the same reply (`limitsInfo`): `status`, `rateLimitType` and
  `resetsAt` from `status`, `representative-claim` and `reset`, and
  `5h`, `7d` and `7d_oi` as `unifiedWindows` `five_hour`, `seven_day`
  and `seven_day_overage_included`, Claude Code's own mapping. The
  bridge's claudeLimits and NoteClaudeLimits take it unchanged.
- A share that doesn't parse is a window not told, never one unused;
  headers with no share and no refusal tell nothing.
- docs/subsystems/claude-subscription-bridge.md describes `{limits}`.

Tests:
- TestTapTellsLimits: a `{limits}` line holding the headers of a real
  reply, on a setup-token account, is told with the same `status`,
  `rateLimitType`, `resetsAt` and `unifiedWindows` as Claude Code
  2.1.309's own `-p` `rate_limit_event` for that account.
- TestTapLimitsUnsaid: no share, an empty or unparsable share, a refusal
  with no window, one window of two.

Run, rebased on origin/main 6b8134430, on macOS arm64:
- gofmt -l clean; go vet ./internal/claudetui, GOOS=linux go vet -tags
  nogui and GOOS=windows go vet of it.
- go test ./internal/claudetui ok; go test -tags nogui ./internal/gateway -run on Claude limits, rate and usage: ok.
- Earlier, on 8af751987: go vet and builds for darwin, linux (nogui) and
  windows, and go test -tags nogui ./...: ok except
  TestProxyCheckSaysAProxyPassedBy (gui) and TestGitSignInRefusedSaysSo
  (library), which fail the same at origin/main without this change.
- Deployed as 0.1.2796 plus this on two gateways: the NAS above
  (setup-token account) and a Linux arm64 VM (browser sign-in). After
  one request each, `magpie quota` on a third computer shows both
  accounts' 5h and 7d with their resets; the setup-token one showed
  none before.

Broken by hand: with the `{limits}` line read but not told
(`&& false`), TestTapTellsLimits goes red.

Not tried: Windows and macOS hosts running the bridge; a 429 reply
through the tap (the refusal case is covered in limitsInfo only).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
